Package: stemflux
Type: Package
Title: Window Selection, Empirical Precision and Detection Limits for
    Chamber Flux Data Processed with 'goFlux'
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Jonathan", "Gewirtzman", email = "jongewirtzman@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Extends the 'goFlux' package (Rheault et al. 2024,
    <doi:10.21105/joss.06393>) with tools developed while processing tree-stem,
    soil and water chamber measurements: stacked-panel (CO2 + CH4) manual
    window selection, non-interactive window detection from the CO2 rise,
    windows built from notebook times, empirical per-measurement precision
    (Allan deviation of first differences, robust MAD variant, quietest-window
    scan), minimum detectable flux by several published methods with
    below-detection flags, a chamber-contamination screen on the starting
    concentration, a PDF exporter compatible with 'ggplot2' >= 3.5, handling of
    analyzer clock resets and interleaved data streams, ebullition (bubble)
    detection and partitioning, and import helpers for very large LI-7810
    files. All functions keep 'goFlux' column conventions so they slot into an
    existing 'goFlux' pipeline.
